{%- comment -%}
  ============================================================================
  dev-compare — "How we compare" modal
  ============================================================================

  DATA SOURCE CHANGED — product.metafields.larke.compare IS NO LONGER READ.

  This section used to render from the product's `larke.compare` metaobject
  (compare -> competitors -> compare_competitor -> rows -> compare_row) and
  guarded the whole overlay on that metafield existing. It does not any more.
  Nothing in this file touches product.metafields.larke.compare, and no code
  path resurrects it. If you grepped for that metafield and landed here: this
  note is the answer, the metaobject is dead as far as the storefront is
  concerned, and you should not wire it back up.

  WHY: the owner asked for a single source of truth that they can edit without
  leaving the theme editor. Two authoring surfaces (metaobject + section
  settings) meant the modal could disagree with itself depending on which one
  was touched last, and a metaobject edit produced no theme diff for review.
  The competitors are now section BLOCKS, so the live content is committed in
  templates/product.json, is reviewable in a diff, and is editable in the
  theme editor by anyone. The overlay is guarded on section.blocks.size
  instead — a product template with no competitor blocks ships nothing at all,
  exactly as the metafield guard used to.

  Contract with assets/dev-compare.js (do not rename any of it): #compare-modal,
  [data-open] on the root, [data-compare-open], [data-compare-close],
  [data-compare-tab="<key>"], [data-compare-panel="<key>"], .dev-compare__panel,
  .dev-compare__panel-content, .dev-compare__toggle-indicator, the ARIA tablist
  roles, aria-selected, tabindex, and [hidden] on inactive panels. Tab and panel
  keys are the competitor name run through | handleize.
  ============================================================================
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- if section.blocks.size > 0 -%}
{{ 'dev-compare.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}
<script src="{{ 'dev-compare.js' | asset_url }}" defer></script>

{%- liquid
  # Content is theme-authored now (see the note above): heading falls back through the
  # section setting to a hardcoded string so the modal can never render an empty <h2>.
  assign heading = section.settings.heading | default: 'How we compare'
  assign close_label = 'actions.close' | t
  assign backdrop_opacity = section.settings.backdrop_opacity | divided_by: 100.0
  assign is_open = section.settings.open_on_load

  # Competitor wordmark treatment.
  #
  # This used to DARKEN the marks (brightness < 1). That was the wrong direction: the logos
  # ship at #3F3F3F, so darkening drove them towards black — which on a cream panel reads as
  # crisp and deliberate, i.e. it made them look BETTER, not worse. The brief is the opposite:
  # the competitor marks should look dull and washed out next to the Larke green.
  #
  # So the treatment now fades them TOWARDS the panel instead of away from it:
  #   contrast < 1  flattens the ink towards mid-grey (kills the crisp black)
  #   opacity  < 1  lets the cream panel bleed through (kills the presence)
  # One slider drives both. At dim 65 the #3F3F3F ink lands near #9C9B98 over the cream —
  # a flat, tired grey against a saturated green.
  #
  # The 100.0 is load-bearing throughout: `divided_by: 100` is INTEGER division in Liquid and
  # every value below 100 collapses to 0 — which here would mean opacity(0), invisible logos.
  assign dim = section.settings.comp_logo_dim | default: 65
  assign dim_opacity = dim | times: 65 | divided_by: 100.0
  assign logo_comp_opacity = 100 | minus: dim_opacity | divided_by: 100.0
  assign dim_contrast = dim | times: 55 | divided_by: 100.0
  assign logo_comp_contrast = 100 | minus: dim_contrast | divided_by: 100.0
  assign logo_comp_grayscale = 0
  if section.settings.comp_logo_desaturate
    assign logo_comp_grayscale = 1
  endif
-%}

{%- comment -%}
  Design tokens from Figma (45075:8383 desktop / 44837:5678 mobile). Everything here is
  fixed except the three --logo-comp-* tokens at the bottom, which are merchant-controlled
  because competitor artwork arrives at whatever lightness the brand publishes.
{%- endcomment -%}
<style>
  .dev-compare {

    {%- comment -%} Desktop modal is a centred card 568px wide (600px Figma frame − 16px inset each side).
       Mobile is a full-bleed bottom sheet, so --modal-max is not applied there. {%- endcomment -%}
    --modal-max: 568px;
    --modal-radius: 32px;
    --sheet-radius: 16px; {%- comment -%} mobile: only the top corners are rounded {%- endcomment -%}
    --card-radius: 16px;
    --badge-radius: 8px;
    --toggle-radius: 32px;

    --pad: 32px;
    --pad-mobile: 24px;

    --heading-size: 32px;        {%- comment -%} Desktop/Title 3 {%- endcomment -%}
    --heading-size-mobile: 24px; {%- comment -%} Mobile/Title 3 {%- endcomment -%}
    --heading-weight: 500;
    --heading-lh: 1.2;

    --toggle-size: 16px;
    --label-size: 16px;
    --label-size-mobile: 14px;
    --value-size: 18px;          {%- comment -%} Lg body {%- endcomment -%}
    --value-size-mobile: 16px;   {%- comment -%} Md body {%- endcomment -%}
    --badge-size: 14px;          {%- comment -%} S body {%- endcomment -%}
    --footnote-size: 16px;
    --footnote-size-mobile: 13px;
    --weight-bold: 700;
    --weight-medium: 500;
    --body-lh: 1.4;

    --icon-size: 24px;
    --logo-w: 110px;
    --logo-h: 33px;
    --logo-larke-h: 33.016px;

    --gap-xs: 4px;
    --gap-sm: 8px;
    --gap-md: 12px;
    --gap-lg: 24px;
    --grid-offset: 40px; {%- comment -%} toggle → grid: 16px flex gap + 24px grid top-padding in Figma {%- endcomment -%}

    {%- comment -%} Fixed palette from the Figma tokens (not merchant-controlled — fidelity). {%- endcomment -%}
    --divider: #D8D1C0;
    --check: #4EA448;          {%- comment -%} Green/900 {%- endcomment -%}
    --cross: #AF0000;
    --card-larke-bg: #FCF5E3;  {%- comment -%} Cream/100 {%- endcomment -%}
    --card-comp-bg: #EFEFEF;
    --toggle-track-bg: #FCF5E3;
    --toggle-active-bg: #FFFFFF;
    --badge-border: #333333;

    {%- comment -%} Open/close motion mirrors the product's size & season guides: a right-side drawer
       that arrives on a decelerating curve and leaves briskly (asymmetric on purpose).
       Same token names and values as dev-main-product so the two popups move identically. {%- endcomment -%}
    --drawer-inset: 16px; {%- comment -%} the panel floats this far off each viewport edge (desktop) {%- endcomment -%}
    --guide-in: 480ms;
    --guide-out: 300ms;
    --ease-out: cubic-bezier(0.22, 1, 0.36, 1);
    --ease-in: cubic-bezier(0.55, 0, 1, 0.45);

    {%- comment -%} Toggle-indicator slide only. {%- endcomment -%}
    --transition: 300ms;

    {%- comment -%} --- Competitor wordmark treatment (merchant-controlled) ---------------------
       Competitor logos are supplied as the brands' own full-colour marks. In the Figma
       comp they read as flat, washed-out grey, so they sit visually *behind* the Larke
       mark instead of competing with it — and so three unrelated brand palettes don't
       turn the panel into a colour clash. It is a setting because every brand's artwork
       starts at a different lightness: a mark that is already pale needs very little
       dimming, a dense black one needs 70%+ before it stops looking deliberate.
         --logo-comp-grayscale  1 = desaturate, 0 = leave the brand colours alone
         --logo-comp-opacity    computed above; dim 65% → 0.5775
         --logo-comp-contrast   computed above; dim 65% → 0.6425

       Both fall out of the single `comp_logo_dim` slider, so there is one knob to turn and
       the two effects can never be set against each other (a flattened mark at full opacity
       just looks blurry; a faded mark at full contrast still reads as crisp). {%- endcomment -%}
    --logo-comp-grayscale: {{ logo_comp_grayscale }};
    --logo-comp-opacity: {{ logo_comp_opacity }};
    --logo-comp-contrast: {{ logo_comp_contrast }};
  }
</style>

{%- comment -%} Reusable inline icons (Figma Icon/Outline/check-circle + x-circle, stroke-width 1.4). {%- endcomment -%}
{%- capture icon_check -%}
<svg class="dev-compare__icon dev-compare__icon--check" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M9 12L11 14L15 10M21 12C21 16.9706 16.9706 21 12 21C7.02944 21 3 16.9706 3 12C3 7.02944 7.02944 3 12 3C16.9706 3 21 7.02944 21 12Z" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.4" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>
{%- endcapture -%}
{%- capture icon_x -%}
<svg class="dev-compare__icon dev-compare__icon--x" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M10 14L12 12M12 12L14 10M12 12L10 10M12 12L14 14M21 12C21 16.9706 16.9706 21 12 21C7.02944 21 3 16.9706 3 12C3 7.02944 7.02944 3 12 3C16.9706 3 21 7.02944 21 12Z" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.4" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>
{%- endcapture -%}

{%- comment -%}
  Overlay, not a page section: hidden + inert + aria-hidden by default so it takes no space and
  cannot be focused until it opens. Open state lives in ONE place — [data-open] on the root —
  which dev-compare.js flips and which QA can flip with plain JS. The PDP triggers carry
  aria-controls="compare-modal" + data-compare-open; that id is a contract — do not rename it.
{%- endcomment -%}
<div
  id="compare-modal"
  class="dev-compare"
  role="dialog"
  aria-modal="true"
  aria-labelledby="compare-modal-title"
  data-open="{% if is_open %}true{% else %}false{% endif %}"
  {% unless is_open %}aria-hidden="true" inert{% endunless %}
  style="
    --bg: {{ section.settings.background_color }};
    --color: {{ section.settings.text_color }};
    --backdrop: {{ section.settings.backdrop_color }};
    --backdrop-opacity: {{ backdrop_opacity }};
  "
>
  <div class="dev-compare__backdrop" data-compare-close></div>

  <div class="dev-compare__panel" tabindex="-1">
    <div class="dev-compare__header">
      <h2 class="dev-compare__title" id="compare-modal-title">{{ heading | escape }}</h2>

      <button type="button" class="dev-compare__close" aria-label="{{ close_label | escape }}" data-compare-close>
        <svg class="dev-compare__close-icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
          <path d="M7 17L17 7M7 7L17 17" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.4" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/>
        </svg>
      </button>
    </div>

    <div class="dev-compare__body">
      <div class="dev-compare__inner">
        {%- comment -%}
          Segmented toggle — one competitor active at a time; the white indicator slides.
          The tab loop and the panel loop below MUST derive `key` identically: it is the id
          glue (compare-tab-<key> / compare-panel-<key>) that dev-compare.js pairs on.
          A blank name would handleize to '' and produce duplicate ids across blocks, so a
          positional fallback keeps every block addressable even while it is being authored.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        <div class="dev-compare__toggle" role="tablist" aria-label="Compare Larke against">
          <span class="dev-compare__toggle-indicator" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          {%- for block in section.blocks -%}
            {%- liquid
              assign key = block.settings.name | handleize
              if key == blank
                assign key = 'competitor-' | append: forloop.index
              endif
            -%}
            <button
              type="button"
              class="dev-compare__toggle-btn"
              role="tab"
              id="compare-tab-{{ key }}"
              data-compare-tab="{{ key }}"
              aria-controls="compare-panel-{{ key }}"
              aria-selected="{% if forloop.first %}true{% else %}false{% endif %}"
              tabindex="{% if forloop.first %}0{% else %}-1{% endif %}"
            >
              {{- block.settings.name | default: 'Competitor' | escape -}}
            </button>
          {%- endfor -%}
        </div>

        {%- for block in section.blocks -%}
          {%- liquid
            assign key = block.settings.name | handleize
            if key == blank
              assign key = 'competitor-' | append: forloop.index
            endif
            assign comp_name = block.settings.name | default: 'Competitor'

            # Logo: an uploaded override always wins, otherwise fall back to one of the
            # wordmarks bundled in /assets. image_picker gives an Image drop, which needs
            # image_url; the bundled files are plain theme assets, which need asset_url —
            # the two are not interchangeable, hence the branch rather than one filter.
            assign comp_logo_src = ''
            if block.settings.logo != blank
              assign comp_logo_src = block.settings.logo | image_url: width: 220
            elsif block.settings.logo_asset != blank
              assign comp_logo_src = block.settings.logo_asset | asset_url
            endif
          -%}
          <div
            class="dev-compare__panel-content"
            role="tabpanel"
            id="compare-panel-{{ key }}"
            data-compare-panel="{{ key }}"
            aria-labelledby="compare-tab-{{ key }}"
            {% unless forloop.first %}hidden{% endunless %}
            {{ block.shopify_attributes }}
          >
            <div class="dev-compare__logos">
              <span class="dev-compare__logo dev-compare__logo--larke">
                <img src="{{ 'dev-compare-logo-larke.svg' | asset_url }}" width="110" height="33" alt="Larke" loading="lazy">
              </span>
              <span class="dev-compare__logo dev-compare__logo--comp">
                {%- if comp_logo_src != blank -%}
                  <img src="{{ comp_logo_src }}" width="110" height="33" alt="{{ comp_name | escape }}" loading="lazy">
                {%- endif -%}
              </span>
            </div>

            {%- comment -%}
              Four fixed row slots. The LABEL is a section setting (all competitors compare on
              the same four axes, so the labels are authored once), the VALUES are per block.
              Both are read by bracket access on a key built from the loop index — four
              near-identical copies of this markup was the alternative.
              A row whose Larke *and* competitor values are both blank is skipped entirely, so
              a competitor with only three meaningful rows doesn't render a hollow fourth.
            {%- endcomment -%}
            <div class="dev-compare__rows">
              {%- for i in (1..4) -%}
                {%- liquid
                  assign k_label = 'row_' | append: i | append: '_label'
                  assign k_larke = 'r' | append: i | append: '_larke'
                  assign k_badge = 'r' | append: i | append: '_badge'
                  assign k_comp = 'r' | append: i | append: '_comp'

                  assign row_label = section.settings[k_label]
                  assign row_larke = block.settings[k_larke]
                  assign row_badge = block.settings[k_badge]
                  assign row_comp = block.settings[k_comp]
                -%}
                {%- if row_larke == blank and row_comp == blank -%}
                  {%- continue -%}
                {%- endif -%}
                <div class="dev-compare__row">
                  <p class="dev-compare__row-label">{{ row_label | escape }}</p>
                  <div class="dev-compare__cells">
                    <div class="dev-compare__cell dev-compare__cell--larke">
                      <div class="dev-compare__cell-main">
                        {{ icon_check }}
                        <p class="dev-compare__value">{{ row_larke | escape }}</p>
                      </div>
                      {%- comment -%}
                        The badge span is only emitted when it has text. It is an outlined pill,
                        so an empty one is not invisible — it renders as a bare 1px rectangle,
                        which is exactly the artefact in the client's mockup.
                      {%- endcomment -%}
                      {%- if row_badge != blank -%}
                        <span class="dev-compare__badge">{{ row_badge | escape }}</span>
                      {%- endif -%}
                    </div>
                    <div class="dev-compare__cell dev-compare__cell--comp">
                      <div class="dev-compare__cell-main">
                        {{ icon_x }}
                        <p class="dev-compare__value dev-compare__value--comp">{{ row_comp | escape }}</p>
                      </div>
                    </div>
                  </div>
                </div>
              {%- endfor -%}
            </div>

            {%- comment -%}
              Two footnote lines, each its own <p> so they wrap and space as separate
              paragraphs rather than one run of text broken by a <br>. The wrapper is only
              emitted when at least one line has content — an empty flex container still
              contributes its parent's 24px gap and would leave a visible hole under the rows.
            {%- endcomment -%}
            {%- if block.settings.footnote_1 != blank or block.settings.footnote_2 != blank -%}
              <div class="dev-compare__footnotes">
                {%- if block.settings.footnote_1 != blank -%}
                  <p class="dev-compare__footnote">{{ block.settings.footnote_1 | escape }}</p>
                {%- endif -%}
                {%- if block.settings.footnote_2 != blank -%}
                  <p class="dev-compare__footnote">{{ block.settings.footnote_2 | escape }}</p>
                {%- endif -%}
              </div>
            {%- endif -%}
          </div>
        {%- endfor -%}
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
{%- endif -%}

{%- comment -%}
  The preset deliberately ships ZERO blocks. Dropping this section onto a template gives an
  empty (and therefore invisible) modal on purpose: the real competitor content — Woolroom,
  R&F, Simba, with the priced-and-dated claims — lives in templates/product.json, where it is
  committed, diffable and reviewable. Starter blocks here would be a second, silently stale
  copy of legally-sensitive comparative pricing, and whichever one a merchant edited would be
  the wrong one. Copy from templates/product.json instead.

  Note also: the schema tag below must be STRICTLY valid JSON — no comments, no trailing
  commas — which is why this explanation sits outside it.
{%- endcomment -%}
{% schema %}
{
  "name": "How we compare",
  "tag": "section",
  "settings": [
    { "type": "header", "content": "Content" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "heading", "label": "Heading", "default": "How we compare", "info": "The modal title." },

    { "type": "header", "content": "Row labels" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "row_1_label", "label": "Row 1 label", "default": "Price" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "row_2_label", "label": "Row 2 label", "default": "Filling" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "row_3_label", "label": "Row 3 label", "default": "Free Trial" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "row_4_label", "label": "Row 4 label", "default": "Warranty" },

    { "type": "header", "content": "Competitor logos" },
    { "type": "range", "id": "comp_logo_dim", "min": 0, "max": 90, "step": 5, "unit": "%", "label": "Competitor logo dimming", "default": 65, "info": "Fades competitor wordmarks towards the panel so they read as flat grey next to the Larke mark. 0% leaves the artwork as supplied; higher is duller." },
    { "type": "checkbox", "id": "comp_logo_desaturate", "label": "Desaturate competitor logos", "default": true, "info": "Strips brand colour so three unrelated palettes don't clash." },

    { "type": "header", "content": "Colors" },
    { "type": "color", "id": "background_color", "label": "Background", "default": "#FFFCF4" },
    { "type": "color", "id": "text_color", "label": "Text color", "default": "#333333" },
    { "type": "color", "id": "backdrop_color", "label": "Backdrop color", "default": "#333333" },
    { "type": "range", "id": "backdrop_opacity", "min": 0, "max": 100, "step": 5, "unit": "%", "label": "Backdrop opacity", "default": 40, "info": "No scrim was authored in Figma — set to taste." },

    { "type": "header", "content": "Layout" },
    { "type": "checkbox", "id": "open_on_load", "label": "Open on page load", "default": false, "info": "Preview only — lets the modal be designed in the editor. Leave off in production." }
  ],
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "competitor",
      "name": "Competitor",
      "limit": 5,
      "settings": [
        { "type": "text", "id": "name", "label": "Name", "info": "Shown on the toggle. Also generates the tab/panel ids — keep it unique." },
        { "type": "image_picker", "id": "logo", "label": "Logo override", "info": "Optional. Overrides the bundled logo below." },
        {
          "type": "select",
          "id": "logo_asset",
          "label": "Bundled logo",
          "default": "",
          "options": [
            { "value": "", "label": "None" },
            { "value": "dev-compare-logo-woolroom.svg", "label": "Woolroom" },
            { "value": "dev-compare-logo-rise-and-fall.svg", "label": "Rise & Fall" },
            { "value": "dev-compare-logo-simba.svg", "label": "Simba" }
          ]
        },

        { "type": "header", "content": "Row 1" },
        { "type": "text", "id": "r1_larke", "label": "Larke value" },
        { "type": "text", "id": "r1_badge", "label": "Badge", "info": "Leave blank to hide the badge." },
        { "type": "text", "id": "r1_comp", "label": "Competitor value" },

        { "type": "header", "content": "Row 2" },
        { "type": "text", "id": "r2_larke", "label": "Larke value" },
        { "type": "text", "id": "r2_badge", "label": "Badge", "info": "Leave blank to hide the badge." },
        { "type": "text", "id": "r2_comp", "label": "Competitor value" },

        { "type": "header", "content": "Row 3" },
        { "type": "text", "id": "r3_larke", "label": "Larke value" },
        { "type": "text", "id": "r3_badge", "label": "Badge", "info": "Leave blank to hide the badge." },
        { "type": "text", "id": "r3_comp", "label": "Competitor value" },

        { "type": "header", "content": "Row 4" },
        { "type": "text", "id": "r4_larke", "label": "Larke value" },
        { "type": "text", "id": "r4_badge", "label": "Badge", "info": "Leave blank to hide the badge." },
        { "type": "text", "id": "r4_comp", "label": "Competitor value" },

        { "type": "header", "content": "Footnotes" },
        { "type": "text", "id": "footnote_1", "label": "Footnote line 1" },
        { "type": "text", "id": "footnote_2", "label": "Footnote line 2", "default": "Valid as of 2026*" }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "presets": [
    { "name": "How we compare", "blocks": [] }
  ]
}
{% endschema %}
